Subject: Justification for Cantor M2B Platform Preflight Fault Provenance Revision

& [Claim] is corrective
  + [statement] revise pure forms before runtime so local observation rejection is never reported as an operating-system error
  + [confidence] is high

& [Support] is concrete
  + [official_semantics] final-path buffer insufficiency returns required size rather than the ordinary zero-failure shape
  + [local_processing] UTF-16 decoding and semantic form validation occur after API success
  + [current_gap] profile 0.1 has no result for either condition
  + [request_gap] no strict pre-effect request currently exposes the shared root grammar

& [WhyRevision] is honesty preserving
  + [false_option] assign ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER or ERROR_INVALID_DATA when the API did not report that error
  + [rejection] a familiar numeric code does not make invented provenance true
  + [solution] a distinct local observation fault class preserves causal origin

& [WhyBeforeRuntime] is security preserving
  + [reason] runtime implementation would otherwise normalize inconvenient outputs into a misleading OS-fault channel
  + [result] every later unsafe branch has a predeclared honest output

& [Counterarguments] are answered
  + [counterargument] use Result outside the serialized record
  + [answer] the serialized proof surface would still omit a materially possible terminal state
  + [counterargument] local invalid data cannot happen on Windows
  + [answer] bounded programs must represent invalid and oversized observations without assuming their impossibility

& [Invalidation] is explicit
  + [condition] source change, provenance collapse, partial evidence, legacy admission, effect surface, failed gate, or stale evidence
  + [response] stop and reprocess before runtime selection

& [Rollback] is direct
  + [module] restore profile 0.1 constant and remove request and observation-fault vocabulary
  + [state] no migration or physical state exists
